L361: # Thank you for your time!
L362: **Supplemental methods**
L363: Ozone-based chemiluminescence
L364: Before analysis, plasma samples were deproteinised using cold ethanol that was first chilled to
L365: 0 °C. 250 µl of each plasma sample was placed in a 1.5 ml microcentrifuge tube and 500 µl of
L366: cold ethanol was added and the tubes were then vortexed for 10 seconds. The tubes were then
L367: centrifuged at 14,000 RPM for 5 minutes. The supernatant was removed to a pre-labelled tube.
L368: Urine and saliva samples were diluted to 1:100 in deionized water prior to the analysis.
L369: Deproteinised plasma and diluted saliva samples were used for the determination of NO3 [-] and
L370: NO2 [-], while diluted urine samples were used for the determination of NO3 [-] by ozone based
L371: chemiluminescence (NOA 280i, Analytix, UK). The standard curve for both NO3 [-] and NO2 [- ]
L372: was created to calculate the concentrations of NO3 [-] and NO2 [-] . The diluted samples were
L373: injected into the purge vessel with an injection volume ranging from 10 µl to 100 µl. The
L374: quality of the peaks was checked visually. Samples were re-diluted with a higher dilution factor
L375: (1:20) if no peaks were detected. The area under the curve of each peak was used to calculate
L376: the concentration of NO3 [-] and NO2 [-] . Samples were analysed in singlicate and analyses were
L377: repeated for samples with low quality peaks. The quality of peaks was checked visually based
L378: on height, fronting and tailing. The calculations were based on the AUCs calculated
L379: automatically for each peak by the software which minimise the risk of between-operator
L380: differences in the calculation of the results.
L381: Salivary nitrite strips
L382: Berkeley strips (Berkeley Test®, CA, USA) were used as per the manufacturer's guidelines.
L383: Specifically, participants were asked to place the test strip with the ‘saliva here’ side on the
L384: tongue and swab it over a 10 s period covering different areas including the dorsal surface of
L385: the tongue. The two ends of the strip were folded and pressed gently for 10 s. The colour of the
L386: NO test pad was then allowed to develop over a 45 s period. The intensity of the colour was
L387: compared with a colour chart included in the product package (Depleted, Low, Threshold,
L388: Target and High), with darker colours corresponding to higher NO2 [−] concentrations. For the
L389: purpose of quantitative analysis, categorical colours were given a categorical number from 1
L390: to 5, where 1 corresponding to “Depleted” and 5 corresponding to “High”. Participants were
L391: asked to repeat a similar procedure at home as required by the study protocol.
[26ms]

